# CakePHP Broadcasting

## Documentation First

Prefer Broadcasting docs (`docs/index.md`). When configuring the WebSocket server, Echo `wsHost`/`wsPort`/`wsPath`, or BlazeCast app id/key/secret, also follow BlazeCast docs and the `blazecast-development` skill.

## Installation

```bash
composer require crustum/broadcasting
```

```bash
{{ assist.cakeCommand('plugin load Crustum/Broadcasting') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('manifest install --plugin Crustum/Broadcasting') }}
```

Creates `config/broadcasting.php` and `config/channels.php`, copies migrations if needed, and appends config load in bootstrap.

## Drivers

Default connection uses `Crustum/Broadcasting.Pusher` with `key` / `secret` / `app_id`. For self-hosted Pusher protocol, set `options.host` / `port` / `path` / `scheme` to the running BlazeCast (or other) server and keep credentials aligned with that server’s apps. Also available: Redis, Log, Null (Null avoids real sends when not using the test trait).

## Defining Broadcast Events

Implement `Crustum\Broadcasting\Event\BroadcastableInterface`:

- `broadcastChannel()` — `Channel`, `PrivateChannel`, `PresenceChannel`, or array
- `broadcastEvent()` — name Echo listens for
- `broadcastData()` — payload array (or null)
- `broadcastSocket()` — optional socket id exclusion

Fire with `broadcast(new ServerCreated($user))` (`use function Crustum\Broadcasting\broadcast`).

Optional `QueueableInterface` for `broadcastQueue()` / queue connection. Conditions via docs (`broadcastWhen`-style APIs). Prefer docs for queue adapter details.

## Authorizing Channels

Register callbacks (or channel classes) in `config/channels.php` with `Broadcasting::channel(...)`. Private/presence require auth; public does not.

Plugin routes: `/broadcasting/auth` (and `/broadcasting/user-auth`). CSRF: follow docs so SPA auth posts succeed. Presence auth returns member data for the join payload.

## Broadcasting Events

- Facade/helpers: `Broadcasting::to(...)->event(...)->data(...)->send()` and `broadcast($event)`
- `toOthers()` — exclude current socket (`X-Socket-ID` / Echo socket id)
- Connection override when multiple broadcasters are configured
- Anonymous events without a dedicated event class — see docs

## Model Broadcasting

On the Table: implement `BroadcastingTraitInterface`, use `Model\Trait\BroadcastingTrait`, add behavior `Crustum/Broadcasting.Broadcasting` with event map (`Model.afterSave` → `saved`, etc.). Configure channels/payload via `setBroadcastChannels` / `setBroadcastPayload` (or behavior config). Disable with table helpers when tests must not emit model broadcasts.

## Client (Echo)

Auth endpoint: `/broadcasting/auth`. Match Echo `key`, `wsHost`, `wsPort`, `wssPort`, `wsPath`, and TLS flags to the Broadcasting driver options and the WebSocket server. Listen/leave/presence join APIs are in Broadcasting docs + Echo docs.

## Notifications over Broadcast

For `via()` broadcast notifications install `crustum/notification-broadcasting` and follow that package’s docs / `broadcasting-notification-development` skill.

## Testing

Use `Crustum\Broadcasting\TestSuite\BroadcastingTrait` on the test case. It swaps in `TestBroadcaster` / `TestQueueAdapter` so broadcasts are captured instead of sent.

Primary asserts (see docs Testing / Available Assertions):

- `assertBroadcastSent` / `assertBroadcastNotSent` / `assertNoBroadcastsSent`
- `assertBroadcastSentTimes` / `assertBroadcastCount`
- `assertBroadcastSentToChannel` / `assertBroadcastSentToChannels` / `assertBroadcastNotSentToChannel`
- `assertBroadcastPayloadContains` / `assertBroadcastPayloadEquals`
- `assertBroadcastSentViaConnection`
- `assertBroadcastExcludedSocket`
- `assertBroadcastQueued` / `assertBroadcastQueuedToChannel` / `assertNoBroadcastsQueued` / `assertBroadcastQueuedCount`

Helpers: `getBroadcastsByEvent(...)` for raw captured payloads. Full examples live in `docs/index.md` § Testing.

## Common Pitfalls

- Private/presence channels without `config/channels.php` auth callbacks.
- Queued broadcasts without a running queue worker.
- Echo `wsHost` / port / `wsPath` / key out of sync with Broadcasting driver options or the WebSocket server.
- App id/key/secret mismatch between Broadcasting config and the WS server applications.
- Tests that hit a real driver — use `BroadcastingTrait` (or Null) so broadcasts are captured/disabled.
- Model broadcasting without both the model trait/interface and the `Broadcasting` behavior.
